# Figma workflow

The UI Kit library is **❖ SberUm UI**:
https://www.figma.com/design/3sLyD0uikSYhlQMoyMCRdV/✦-SberUm-UI

When mapping a product frame to code, look up components and variables in that library first (`search_design_system` with that file, scoped to its libraryKey).

When a Figma frame or selection is provided, inspect it through Figma MCP before implementing it.

Do not infer the design from a screenshot if structured Figma context is available.

Before implementation extract:

- frame hierarchy;
- layout structure;
- Auto Layout behavior;
- component instances;
- component properties;
- variants;
- variables;
- typography;
- spacing;
- assets;
- repeated patterns.

# Design interpretation

Figma is the visual source of truth.

❖ SberUm UI is the component implementation source of truth.

Therefore:

Figma answers:
"What should this experience look like?"

UI Kit answers:
"How should this component be implemented?"

# Conflicts

If Figma and the UI Kit disagree:

do not silently resolve the discrepancy.

Prefer the existing UI Kit implementation for shared component behavior and report the mismatch.

# Implementation plan

Before writing code, provide a short mapping:

Figma → UI Kit

Example:

Button / Primary / Medium
→ Button variant="primary" size="md"

Input / Default
→ Input

Modal
→ Modal

Avatar
→ Avatar

Then implement the prototype.
